\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
For every fixed $A\geq 1$, is finding a directed feedback vertex set within factor A NP-hard on explicitly given unweighted digraphs, with a positive threshold and a deterministic polynomial-time gap reduction?

\subsection{Short English statement}
For every fixed $A\geq 1$, is finding a directed feedback vertex set within factor A NP-hard on explicitly given unweighted digraphs, with a positive threshold and a deterministic polynomial-time gap reduction?

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] OpenAI, manuscript citation page. Source of the formulation motivating this local problem.
\url{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/Constant-factor-hardness-of-directed-feedback-vertex-set-September-23-2026/README.md}.
\end{itemize}

